What’s ROS 2- Jazzy? # type: ignore 
•	ROS 2 Jazzy Jalisco is a long-term support (LTS) distribution of the Robot Operating System 2. It was released by Open Robotics in May 2024 and is supported until May 2029. A ROS 2 distribution is a tested set of ROS client libraries, command-line tools, middleware integrations, build tools, and packages released together under a fixed name and version policy.# type: ignore 
•	Jazzy is the first ROS 2 LTS distribution targeting Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (Noble Numbat). Its platform support policy, including supported architectures and operating systems, is defined in REP 2000. # type: ignore 

Where & How ROS 2 – Jazzy? # type: ignore  
This answers queries about the installation and access of this middle-ware. # type: ignore 

• A computer or virtual machine running Ubuntu 24.04 is needed to proceed. # type: ignore 
Terminal command procedure: # type: ignore 
•	 locale # type: ignore 
•	 sudo apt update && sudo apt install locales. # type: ignore 
•	sudo locale-gen en_US en_US.UTF-8 # type: ignore 
•	sudo update-locale LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8 LANG=en_US.UTF-8 # type: ignore 
•	export LANG=en_US.UTF-8 # type: ignore 
•	verify: locale # type: ignore 
to enable the required repositories: # type: ignore 
•	sudo apt install software-properties-common # type: ignore 
•	sudo add-apt-repository universe # type: ignore 
       adding the ROS 2 GPG key with apt: # type: ignore 
•	sudo apt update && sudo apt install curl -y # type: ignore 
•	sudo curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ros/rosdistro/master/ros.key -o /usr/share/keyrings/ros-archive-keyring.gpg # type: ignore 
Adding the repository to the sources list: # type: ignore 
•	echo "deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/ros-archive-keyring.gpg] http://packages.ros.org/ros2/ubuntu $(. /etc/os-release && echo $UBUNTU_CODENAME) main" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ros2.list > /dev/null # type: ignore 
•	sudo apt update && sudo apt install ros-dev-tools # type: ignore 
•	sudo apt upgrade -y # type: ignore 
•	sudo apt install ros-jazzy-desktop # type: ignore 
Why use a ROS-2 Jazzy? # type: ignore 
•	It is a very helpful tool, especially when documentation is limited in distinction between Humble and Jazzy. It's also good at catching syntax errors.' # type: ignore 
•	Long term support window as a 5 year release as  it provides a stable foundation for production systems and research projects without needing a disruptive version upgrade every year. # type: ignore  
•	Simulates your system before deploying to real hardware & as well as access a rich ecosystem of pre-built packages for navigation, manipulation, vision etc: . # type: ignore 
When use a ROS – 2 Jazzy? # type: ignore 
•	Primarily when an individual need a long term support release with modern platform support , active updates till a definite time period. # type: ignore 
•	Whenever a system needs ubuntu 24.04  environment then ROS 2 Jazzy compatibility will come in handy. # type: ignore 
•	Can be used for physics-based robot simulations as its well suited to Gazebo Harmonic & Gazebo Ionic.# type: ignore 

